#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079407} :activity/id #uuid "a77c2038-5986-582e-a8bb-7584a9cbc0c1" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049999 :topic/id #uuid "256a23e4-f397-590a-a6c9-fc3db20c7990" :topic/math-academy-id 681} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079407 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079673 :tutorial/content "Suppose we want to find the surface area of a cube whose edges are $3\\,\\textrm{cm}$ in length, like the one shown below.\n\n![](images/e7/e727b20f63c46ef6124d2d33f5db0a003d798f69ec988ee6b41b651e34456387.png)\n\nThe surface area of the cube is the area of all the faces combined. In general, for a cube with sides of length $s$, there are $6$ sides, each with area\n\n$$\n\\mathcal A = s^2\n$$\n\nSo, the surface area is given by\n\n$$\nS = 6\\mathcal A =6 s^2\n$$\n\nTo find the surface area of the cube above, we substitute\n\n$$\ns=3 \\: \\textrm{cm}\n$$\n\ninto the formula. This gives\n\n$$\nS = 6(3\\, \\text{cm})^2 = 54 \\,\\textrm{cm}^2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface area of the cube is $54\\,\\textrm{cm}^2$." :tutorial/id #uuid "c7479702-e5c9-52bf-b435-5bf2abc4badf" :tutorial/math-academy-id 4330 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "d6501529-1ab5-5d3b-92df-37ca3469898e" :step/math-academy-id 26344 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079408}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079408 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078498 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078350 :question/id #uuid "d27805b4-9ade-5429-b5d9-85f202750d97" :question/math-academy-id "e-7150"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "45915032-87ea-583d-8570-ad1d56d019b2" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049608}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078703} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078708}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Surface Area of a Cube Given a Side Length"} :step/id #uuid "9a2bf0e8-c18f-5fbe-9ba9-1a20ca1e4443" :step/math-academy-id 26345 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079409}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079409 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078499 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078351 :question/id #uuid "1572978d-d8a9-5a85-b5f7-dc724de52824" :question/math-academy-id "e-7151"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "676d79a5-129d-5e14-ad1f-4af43090459f" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049923}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078709} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078820}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Side Length of a Cube Given the Surface Area"} :step/id #uuid "e0e2bab3-8722-5301-95a1-a279dc7a58f6" :step/math-academy-id 26346 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079442}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079442 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079681 :tutorial/content "The **lateral surface area** of a cube is the surface area of the side faces alone. In other words, it's the surface area that does not include the area of the top or bottom faces.\n\n![](images/78/78fbc4013c4f625f7e5b839ed7545cc6c8a476d31a7f0f5bda8645d73785f70e.png)\n\nThe lateral surface area $S_L$ of a cube can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nS_L = 4s^2\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the length of a side." :tutorial/id #uuid "a6bfc760-f618-5908-a6c0-c66506cc9a1d" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5401 :tutorial/title "Lateral Surface Areas of Cubes"} :step/id #uuid "7197ecf8-70bc-5be5-9a51-287584180e25" :step/math-academy-id 33675 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079443}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079443 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078523 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078376 :question/id #uuid "80eb6640-3bd6-5cff-81c5-7e6b850d6f93" :question/math-academy-id "e-9015"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b01e7b76-466f-522d-bfd1-aa8616cbe023" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078710} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078711}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Lateral Surface Area of a Cube Given its Dimensions"} :step/id #uuid "559b5bfc-80cc-53a7-84a7-48f64981ccbc" :step/math-academy-id 33676}] :activity/title "Surface Areas of Cubes" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186078696}]}
